fix: review round-6 (hardware/repo reviewer) — integrity honesty, L1-drain in scenario A, NOTICE distributors, unified claims

Integrity model (review 4):
- architecture EN/RU/ZH: added explicit "Integrity caveat" -- the "corrupt file ->
  miss -> no wrong output" guarantee rests on recompute-fallback, not on
  per-object checksum detection; no fsync guarantee is claimed (atomic rename
  only covers process-crash, not power loss). Failure-model row itself has the
  pointer to the caveat.

Scenario A methodology (review 2):
- test-recovery.sh: added drain_L1() -- an explicit non-matching-prefix "drain"
  request before scenario A's re-send, plus hard FAIL->INCONCLUSIVE when
  cached_tokens>0 but zero post-mark L2-read events (RAM-only reuse that must
  NOT be credited as disk recovery). Corrected the "TTFT up" column label to
  "TTFT DOWN" in Persistence-and-Recovery x3 (EN/RU/ZH) and mixed
  Retrieved-vs-L2 evidence wording to match the retrieval pattern.

Security (review 6,7,8):
- docs/security.md: "no unauthenticated management endpoints" claim corrected to
  "loopback-only is NOT authentication -- any UID on the same host can reach
  these ports"; README x3 aligned.
- docs/security EN/added: public issues are NOT the reporting channel; enable
  GitHub private vulnerability reporting or contact the maintainer directly.
  (RU/ZH security pages updated likewise.)

LICENSE attribution (review 19):
- NOTICE: attribution term reworded from "anyone who uses" to "anyone who
  DISTRIBUTES" -- aligned with Apache-2.0 §4(d) semantics (es. forks/mirrors/
  assets/bundlings redistribute the Software; mere end-users who only run it
  personal are exempt).

Rest string accuracy (review 14,15):
- final-report EN: added caveat that "the brief" / "the review's protocol" are
  external design docs not present in this repo; generic ops are reproducible
  without them but the exact pass criteria must be adapted per site.
- README (EN): dropped "Universal" from the title (only one model integrated so
  far); added "Model-agnostic core (aspiration; only one model integrated so far)"
  caveat.
- README + benchmarks EN: "100k-1M tokens in seconds" is now explicitly a *goal*
  with named acceptance criteria (median TTFT across >=3 runs, cached_tokens>0
  plus L2/disk read events, physical NVMe byte increase, L1 > largest reuse
  prefix), not a claim.

Capacity-accounting after restart (review 3):
- storage-management EN/RU/ZH: noted that upstream lazy-index built from file
  sizes as touched does NOT guarantee pre-restart files stay inside
  get_usage()/max_capacity_gb; the required hardware test is documented (fill
  cache -> restart -> keep writing -> verify used_bytes bounded).

Integration (review 5):
- wiki Recipes-Integration EN/RU and ZH (2/3 sections directly applied; ZH
  similar): added "Verify the engine geometry before reuse" section to cover the
  prod path KV_PERSIST=1's missing verify-engine-identity gate.